  "treatyAssessment": {
    "partiesApmbcCount": 164,
    "partiesCcmCount": 112,
    "nonPartyHeavyUsers": ["US", "RU", "CN", "IN", "PK", "IR", "IL", "KP", "SY", "EG", "MM", "VN", "LA", "KR"],
    "heavilyContaminatedStates": ["AF", "AO", "BA", "KH", "CO", "HR", "IQ", "LA", "LB", "MM", "SO", "SS", "SD", "SY", "UA", "UZ", "YE", "ZW"],
    "source": "APMBC Art.7 reports + Landmine Monitor annual + ICBL-CMC databases"
  },
  "implicationsForPlatform": [
    "Platform scope = counter-side (detection/clearance/EORE/VA) across both treaty states and non-parties. EORE and VA obligations apply irrespective of treaty status (customary IHL + CRPD).",
    "Data handling must respect national sovereignty: SHA/CHA coords often classified under national security law (e.g., UA, IQ, AF, MM). Tier 3 Preferences() storage + National Mine Action Authority (NMAA) consent gate are required before any cross-border sync.",
    "Procurement of detectors / MDD / flails must comply with dual-use export control regimes (Wassenaar Arrangement, EU Reg 2021/821, US EAR, JP 外為法). Cross-reference `60-apps/etzhayyim-project-resources/content/legal/jp/laws.jsonld` for JP export controls.",
    "Victim assistance data is PII + often disability status — Tier 3 + GDPR Art.9 special categories + national disability law (e.g., JP 障害者基本法, UK Equality Act 2010 s.6).",
    "For states not party to APMBC/CCM, the platform must NOT be used to facilitate treaty-prohibited activities even if domestically lawful. This is enforced by the `validateScope` pipeline step in `20-actors/demining/actor-manifest.jsonld`."
  ],
  "verificationNote": "Dates, law numbers, and session/chapter references above are from widely-cited secondary sources (ICRC IHL database, UN Treaty Collection, Landmine Monitor). For binding legal use, cite primary sources: UN Treaty Series vol. 2056 (APMBC) and vol. 2688 (CCM); national official gazettes for each statute. Entries flagged `verifyCitation: true` require confirmation before publication."
}
